{
  "borough": "London Borough of Barking and Dagenham",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed development would result in the loss of a family-sized dwellinghouse, the need for which is clearly demonstrated in the development plan and supporting evidence base. While it would provide a dwelling in the form of an HMO, it fails to demonstrate that this is an identified need, would cause a loss of local amenity including to neighbouring occupiers. As such, the proposal is considered to have a detrimental impact on the borough&#39;s supply of family housing and is contrary to the following policies:&nbsp;National Planning Policy Framework (December 2024)Policies&nbsp;D6, D14 and T4&nbsp;of the London Plan (March 2021)Policies SP3, SP8, DMD1, DMT1, DMH5 and DMSI3&nbsp;of the Barking and Dagenham Local Plan 2037 (September 2024)",
    "The proposed HMO has the potential to increase activity level and coming and goings to and from the site leading to additional levels of noise and disturbance at the property. The proposal is therefore likely to have a negative impact on neighbouring amenity in this street of family housing and in turn the health and wellbeing of neighbouring residents. As such the proposal is contrary to the following:Policies DMD 1, SP 7 and DMSI 3 of the Local Plan (September 2024)",
    "The proposed development fails to demonstrate&nbsp;that the provided parking proposed for the development could be safely accessed and utilised. The proposal therefore fails to provide safe and accessible parking and fails to comply with the following policies&nbsp;which seek to ensure proposals show how car parking will be designed and managed and to take into consideration on-street parking availability and existing and planned public transport provision:National Planning Policy Framework (December 2024)Policies T1, T6 and T6.1 of the London Plan (March 2021)Policy DMT2 of the Barking and Dagenham Local Plan 2037 (September 2024)"
  ],
